@@ -16,3 +16,11 @@
 3. Publish without force and verify branch HEAD.
 4. Attempt one manual `ios-metal.yml` dispatch; if the current session cannot reach GitHub, preserve the commit and report that exact external blocker rather than claiming a run.
 5. On successful Apple run, inspect full logs and IPA evidence before reporting build success.
+
+## Dispatch attempt — 2026-11-26
+
+- Pushed overlay commit: `5342cfc83b22c24f7d69b476fcaaa5bafda76456`. GitHub compare reports branch `mission-09-final-assembly` identical to that SHA.
+- Independently fetched workflow and materializer at that branch. Workflow has both `host` and `ios-arm64` jobs and no `needs` dependency; materializer expects tree `bc7acad6eaf9d1b185c32ee75b953469bba14063`.
+- GitHub reports no workflow runs for the pushed commit.
+- One manual dispatch attempt with `gh workflow run` failed before contacting the API: `error connecting to api.github.com`. `gh auth status` reports invalid cached token and temporary DNS lookup failure. CUA/browser host is unavailable; GitHub connector exposes no dispatch action.
+- No CI rerun or IPA has been produced. Resume with a manual dispatch after GitHub DNS/auth connectivity is restored; do not infer Apple build success from the passing local suite.
